<title>USA: USDA ups 96/97 US orange output forecast to record.</title>
<headline>USDA ups 96/97 US orange output forecast to record.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Friday raised its forecast for Florida 1996/97 orange production by 1.5 million boxes to 225.7 million boxes.</p>
<p>This is the largest crop produced in Florida, topping the previous record of 206.7 million boxes harvested in 1979-80 and about 10 percent more than last year.</p>
<p>USDA raised its forecast for Florida's record large Valencia crop to 91.5 million boxes from 90.0 million seen in June.</p>
<p>USDA orange production estimates (crop in 1,000 boxes, yield in gallons/box at 42.0 degrees Brix basis):</p>
<p>				    1996/97:	    Indicated</p>
<p>    -		     July	  Prev.Est.    1995/96</p>
<p> Florida Oranges     225,700	 224,200     203,200</p>
<p> Florida Temples	 2,400	   2,400	 2,150</p>
<p> Fla. FCOJ Yield	  1.58	    1.58	  1.52</p>
<p> U.S. Oranges	  299,120	 297,920     271,790</p>
<p>Note-U.S. oranges and Florida oranges exclude temples.</p>
</text>
